# Vlarch release version

When you finish a user-facing change and commit or push to `main`, also bump the repo root `version.txt` (patch increment, e.g. `0.0.111` → `0.0.112`) in the same commit or an immediate follow-up before push.

`version.txt` is what `update.sh`, the CDN, and `vlarch-waybar-update` use to detect new releases. Do not push feature/fix work without updating it unless the user explicitly says to skip versioning.
